<title>USA: St. Jude says Ventritex deal clears FTC.</title>
<headline>St. Jude says Ventritex deal clears FTC.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Jude Medical Inc said the Hart-Scott-Rodino waiting period for its acquisition of Ventritex Inc has ended.</p>
<p>Closing of the roughly $365-million transaction is subject to approval by Ventritex shareholders at a special meeting scheduled for May 12, St. Jude said.</p>
<p>The medical device makers agreed to an amended merger deal last month in which each share of Ventritex will be exchanged for 0.5 share of St. Jude, compared to an earlier exchange ratio of 0.6 share.</p>
<p>The companies said they agreed to the amended value to reflect the impact on Ventritex's business from certain component failures in its Cadence Model V-110 implantable defibrillator.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
